what is functional programming ?
functional programming is transforming of data using functions ,rather than changing state

Why Companies Care (Say This in Interviews)

Functional style helps because it:
reduces bugs caused by shared mutable state
makes concurrent code safer
improves testability
simplifies reasoning about code
fits well with distributed systems and data pipelines
This is why it appears in:

Java Streams
Reactive programming
Kafka Streams
Spark / Flink
LangGraph / workflow engines

| Imperative         | Functional            |
| ------------------ | --------------------- |
| Change state       | Transform data        |
| Loops              | Map / filter / reduce |
| Mutable objects    | Immutable objects     |
| Harder concurrency | Safer concurrency     |


